WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.320
Tesla's third-generation Megapack production start at gigatexas adds 50 gigawatt hours of annual utility-scale storage capacity. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 598. Workers at the Texas gigafactory have started making the latest version of the large battery packs. The site aims to reach 50 gigawatt hours of yearly output aimed at big grid projects. This represents the initial run of the updated Megapack line built for larger installations.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:47.880
At the same time, Tesla is using price adjustments in China to clear out vehicle stock. Cash offers and a 10,000 yuan reduction now apply to Model Y units sitting in inventory. The same steps cover Model 3 stock as well, and come during softer local demand plus lower deliveries.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:58.200
These moves line up with the end of the quarter push to shift existing cars, meanwhile the charging network keeps growing to support both company cars and outside vehicles.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:09.240
Tesla now operates more than 1200 supercharger locations spread across China. The added sites help Tesla drivers and also feed the open access program for other brands.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:21.200
Software development for self-driving has hit another checkpoint in the current version series. The team reached a major step forward inside the V14 updates toward fully unsupervised operation.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:32.140
Real-world use still turns up repeated spots where drivers step in. Most overrides happen during everyday driving along with occasional navigation tweaks and parking maneuvers.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.940
Drivers report staying off the wheel except in those moments and want fixes that keep the hands free mode intact.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:48.100
Terrain changes create extra trouble for the system. Large bumps and quick slope shifts have forced takeovers when the speed stayed too high for the conditions.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:02:00.560
One account mentioned switching modes too late on a bump that could not be handled safely. A separate driver account noted that the vast majority of interventions occurred during routine driving rather than edge cases.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:11.960
Occasional navigation adjustments and parking situations that require wheel contact also trigger overrides. The driver emphasized never touching the wheel outside those specific instances.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:18.260
The report pointed to these moments as the main points where hands free operation gives way to manual control.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:33.140
Another driver described prior FSD difficulties with large bumps or sudden slope changes. Switching to a slower mode too late left the vehicle at 35 miles per hour across terrain that could not be crossed safely at that speed.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:39.420
The account stressed how the slope change left the system's speed mismatched to the actual road surface.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:50.680
Early riders of the cyber cab have begun sharing what the first limited trips in Austin felt like. Feedback describes a lounge style cabin with a big screen and strong audio setup.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:03:01.860
The vehicle has also turned up in Las Vegas outside the original test zone. Real user experiences from the first week of passenger operations were collected and published in a report.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:12.820
The summary aggregates honest reviews from early riders in Austin after limited service began. Owners who tried the vehicle listed desired changes after those early rides.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:24.740
Requests included map manipulation and camera view access to match standard Tesla controls. Seat adjustment sliders, phone casting and emergency override options were also flagged.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:29.760
Arm rest and window behavior adjustments appeared on the same list of suggested improvements.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:42.780
Discussion around the cyber cab highlighted its hardware cost advantage and potential daily earnings. Faster turnarounds, efficient charging and expanded use cases were cited as ways to increase earnings per unit.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:57.040
Community conversation noted sustained excitement around the Robotaxi program overall. A rare roadster was spotted in a random school parking lot. The license plate drew additional attention from observers in the photos shared online.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:09.040
Chinese car companies are taking a different path on robot development. They are pulling motion control and perception tools straight from their vehicle programs into affordable humanoid designs for home use.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:19.300
The shared systems cut research costs and speed up work on balance and handling tasks. Tesla keeps its vehicle software and robot work on separate hardware paths.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:28.420
Car inference runs on current or next silicon tuned for road scenes while the robot uses different joint controllers and manipulation focused data.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:40.760
The split prevents one chip from serving both needs, but also skips the shared team savings that competitors gain. Over time, the bigger edge may come from the data loop rather than the hardware itself.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:54.220
A firm running millions of cars can pull edge case footage at low added cost and reuse it for robot training. Rivals without that fleet must rely more on simulation or pay for equivalent real world miles.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:05:02.320
A Tesla owner in Pennsylvania received a $500 bill for unpaid gas tax even though the car runs on electricity.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:12.640
The letter reflects state moves to bring in new road fees as fuel tax income drops. Similar notices have gone out in other states facing the same revenue shift.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:22.580
Non owners who took model-wide demo drives often shifted their view afterward. They began wondering why they had previously disliked a car they knew little about.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:27.580
The pattern shows direct experience overriding earlier assumptions about the vehicle.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:35.040
Before we go, the next update on how the V14 software handles those reported terrain cases should come through soon.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.820
That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:47.400
